    ev.kobs_check_substrate["Identify the sandbox substrate: gVisor ('/proc/1/comm' looks like 'runsc-sandbox', dmesg shows sentry lines) vs real-kernel microVM (dmesg shows real driver init, 'uname -r' matches a real Linux release, virtio-blk on '/dev/vda')"]
    ev.kobs_check_perf_sysctl["cat /proc/sys/kernel/perf_event_paranoid -- if the file is absent, the kernel was built without CONFIG_PERF_EVENTS or the tool is running under gVisor; if present, its value gates unprivileged access (-1 = anyone, 0/1/2/3 = progressively more restricted)"]
    ev.kobs_check_bpf_mount["ls /sys/fs/bpf -- absent means the bpffs isn't mounted; present with unprivileged bpf() still failing means CAP_BPF / CAP_SYS_ADMIN gate applies"]
    ev.kobs_check_bpf_sysctl["cat /proc/sys/kernel/unprivileged_bpf_disabled -- if absent, no CONFIG_BPF_SYSCALL; if 0, unprivileged bpf() is allowed; if 1 or 2, only CAP_BPF/CAP_SYS_ADMIN holders can use it"]
    ev.kobs_check_ftrace_mount["mount / grep -E 'tracefs/debugfs' AND ls /sys/kernel/tracing /sys/kernel/debug/tracing -- absent both means the guest kernel doesn't expose tracefs, either not compiled in or intentionally hidden"]
    ev.kobs_check_capeff["grep -E '^CapEff' /proc/self/status -- if 0000000000000000 the agent has no effective caps, so CAP_BPF / CAP_SYS_ADMIN / CAP_PERFMON gates cannot be bypassed by the agent uid alone; check whether setpriv to root can elevate ('setpriv --reuid=0 /bin/true')"]
    ev.kobs_check_tool_installed["which perf bpftrace bpftool -- if missing, the tool simply isn't in this rootfs; separate from any kernel-substrate question"]
    cls.kobs_gvisor_substrate{{"gVisor's sentry does not implement the kernel subsystem this tool uses (perf_event_open, ftrace, most of bpf()). No cap change and no sysctl inside the guest lifts this -- the syscall is not wired up."}}
    cls.kobs_microvm_kernel_missing_config{{"Real-kernel microVM but the guest kernel was built without the required config (CONFIG_PERF_EVENTS, CONFIG_BPF_SYSCALL, CONFIG_FTRACE). Cannot be fixed at runtime; requires a different kernel build."}}
    cls.kobs_microvm_caps_gate{{"Real-kernel microVM with the subsystem compiled in, but caps (CAP_BPF / CAP_SYS_ADMIN / CAP_PERFMON) or a paranoid sysctl gate access. The agent uid does not hold the caps; whether setpriv-root helps depends on whether root_caps in the platform's OCI spec includes them."}}
    cls.kobs_tool_not_installed{{"The kernel subsystem is fine; the userspace tool just isn't in the rootfs. Install via distro package manager, verify against the guest's substrate before assuming it will work."}}
    con.kobs_reproduce_outside_sandbox(["For gVisor substrate limitations: reproduce the observability workload against a real-kernel Linux environment outside safeyolo (a real VM, dev workstation, or a CI runner). Do not ask the operator to weaken the sandbox to expose the missing subsystem -- it isn't a policy knob."])
    con.kobs_use_userspace_alternative(["Replace the kernel-obs step with a userspace alternative: 'py-spy' / 'rbspy' for profiling, 'strace -f cmd' for syscall tracing at launch, language-native instrumentation. See [[triage-guest-tools-and-sudo]] for the ptrace-side story."])
    con.kobs_install_tool(["Install the tool via the guest sudo/apt path (see [[triage-guest-tools-and-sudo]] for install semantics) and re-run. Verify against 'ev.kobs_check_substrate' first; installing a kernel-obs tool that the substrate doesn't support wastes budget and time."])
    con.kobs_retry_under_setpriv(["On real-kernel microVM with caps gating access: retry the command under 'setpriv --reuid=0 --regid=0 --clear-groups CMD'. Only works if the OCI root_caps list includes the required cap (CAP_BPF / CAP_SYS_ADMIN / CAP_PERFMON). If setpriv is not the issue, the paranoid sysctl is."])

